# fix symmetry example: SiC with zinc blende structure, Tersoff potential,
# and a two-fold rotation axis along z (space group P2)
#
# Zinc blende is the diamond structure with the two FCC sublattices
# occupied by different elements.  It has no inversion symmetry, since
# inversion would exchange Si and C.  The two-fold rotation about the z
# axis through a Si atom maps each sublattice onto itself.  The Si atoms
# on the axis can only move along z.

units           metal
atom_style      atomic

# basis atoms 1-4 are on one FCC sublattice (Si), 5-8 on the other (C)
lattice         diamond 4.3596
